.TH BOSWAS-WEATHER 1 "November 2026" "boswas-apps 3.0~alpha1" "Boswas OS"
.SH NAME
boswas-weather \- the weather and the forecast for the places you choose
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-weather
.RB [ \-\-place
.IR name ]
.br
.B boswas-weather
.BR \-\-version " | " \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boswas-weather
is Weather, the weather application of the Boswas desktop. Its navigation
pane lists the places you added, in your order; below them are two more
pages.
.TP
.B A place
The conditions now: the condition with its icon (a night icon after
sunset), the temperature, how warm it feels, today's high and low, and
when the forecast was fetched. Below come the next 24 hours (time,
condition, temperature on a curve, chance of rain), cards with the wind
(speed, the direction it comes from, gusts), humidity with the dew point,
air pressure, the UV index and its category, visibility, today's
precipitation, sunrise, sunset and cloud cover, and the next 10 days
(condition, chance of rain, low and high with a bar on the scale of all
ten days).
.TP
.B Manage places
Search for a city or town by name and add it to your places; reorder your
places, remove them (the removal can be taken back) and choose the home
place, which Weather opens with. The first place you add is home until you
choose another. At most 50 places are kept.
.TP
.B Settings
The units: temperature in degrees Celsius or Fahrenheit, wind speed in
kilometers per hour, miles per hour, meters per second or knots,
precipitation in millimeters or inches, pressure in hectopascals or inches
of mercury. The time format (as the system is set, 12-hour or 24-hour). How
often the forecast of the place shown is fetched again while Weather is
open: every 15, 30 or 60 minutes, or never. On a first start the units
follow the locale (the units of the United States where it uses them, else
metric).
.PP
A forecast is fetched when Weather opens, when a place is shown whose
forecast is older than ten minutes, with F5, Ctrl+R or the refresh button,
and at the chosen interval. Only one request per place is made at a time.
The last forecast of every place is kept; when the weather service cannot
be reached, Weather shows it, marked as offline with the time it was
fetched, and offers to try again.
.PP
Only one Weather runs per session; starting it again brings the window
forward and shows the place asked for.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-place " name"
Open with the forecast of one of your places, found by its name (letter
case does not matter). Without the option, or for a name that is not one
of your places, Weather opens with the home place.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a summary of the options and exit.
.SH KEYS
F5 and Ctrl+R fetch the forecast of the place shown again. Ctrl+F opens
Manage places with the cursor in the search box. Ctrl+Tab and
Ctrl+Shift+Tab go through the pages, Ctrl+, opens the settings, Ctrl+W
and Ctrl+Q close Weather. In the navigation pane, Up and Down go from
place to place. In the hourly forecast Left and Right, and in the 10-day
forecast Up and Down, move from hour to hour and from day to day. In
Manage places, Down goes from the search box to the results; on one of
your places Alt+Up and Alt+Down move it and Delete removes it.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/com.boswas.Weather/places.json
Your places, their order and the home place. A file that cannot be read
is set aside as
.I places.json.damaged
and Weather starts without places.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/com.boswas.Weather/settings.json
The settings.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/com.boswas.Weather/forecast-*.json
The last forecast of each place, as the weather service sent it (in metric
units), with the time it was fetched. The files of places that were
removed are deleted when Weather starts.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/com.boswas.Weather/window.ini
The size of the window.
.PP
Every file is written to a temporary file first and then put in place,
so an interrupted write never leaves a broken file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success (also when a running Weather was brought forward); 4 when
started as root, which Weather refuses.
.SH NOTES
Weather data by Open-Meteo.com
.RI ( https://open-meteo.com/ ),
licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 license (CC BY 4.0).
Weather shows this attribution at the bottom of every forecast and in its
settings.
.PP
Weather never uses your location. It asks Open-Meteo
.RI ( geocoding-api.open-meteo.com
and
.IR api.open-meteo.com ,
over HTTPS) for two things only: the places whose name matches what you
type into the search, and the forecast of the coordinates of a place you
added. Requests carry the User-Agent
.B boswas-weather/1.0
and nothing that identifies you: no account, key or cookie. Answers larger
than 2 MB, redirects and answers that do not have the documented form are
refused; a request gives up after 15 seconds. Proxies set in the
environment
.RB ( https_proxy )
are used.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boswas\-clock (1),
.BR boswas\-calendar (1)
